# Cross-Module Semantic Logic Audit

Before implementing Phase 2 enhancements, audit ALL content modules to map existing semantic logic and identify what can be reused vs what needs to be built.

## Task: Comprehensive Semantic Intelligence Inventory

**SEARCH these files:**
- intelligence/content/grade.py (P20 - stance detection)
- intelligence/content/fullread.py (P21 - full-read grading)
- intelligence/content/semantic_read.py (P23 - semantic findings)
- intelligence/content/semantic_frames.py (P24 - frame extraction)

**LOOK FOR these semantic features:**

### 1. Paraphrase/Synonym Systems
- Dictionary structures mapping words to variants
- Synonym lists (increase → rise → grow)
- Verb ↔ Noun mappings (boils → boiling point)
- Domain-specific vocabularies (scientific vs policy)
- Any text expansion or matching logic

### 2. Unit Normalization/Conversion
- Temperature conversions (°C, °F, K, degrees)
- Distance conversions (km, miles, meters)
- Money normalization ($M, million, $1,000,000)
- Percentage formats (8%, "8 percent", 0.08)
- Numeric extraction and parsing
- Unit comparison or standardization

### 3. Condition Recognition/Equivalence
- Condition extraction ("at sea level", "in FY2024")
- Equivalence mappings (sea level = 1 atm = standard pressure)
- Context awareness (altitude, time periods, circumstances)
- Condition comparison logic

### 4. Numeric Tolerance/Comparison
- Tolerance matching (100 ≈ 100.5)
- Percentage-based comparison
- Exact vs approximate matching
- Numeric contradiction detection

### 5. Entity Extraction/Matching
- Named entity recognition
- Entity type classification (location, org, person)
- Entity identity comparison (California ≠ Texas)
- Entity normalization

### 6. Frame-Based Reasoning
- Frame structure definitions
- Component extraction (entity, action, quantity, etc.)
- Frame comparison logic
- Entailment/contradiction detection

### 7. Relationship Detection
- Causal relationships (because, due to)
- Temporal relationships (before, after)
- Conditional relationships (if, when)
- Contrastive relationships (but, however)

### 8. Action/Directional Logic
- Action extraction (increase, decrease)
- Directional cue detection
- Action comparison/alignment
- Negation handling

